"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both JPMorgan and Citi disclose the existence of a formal framework and risk appetite for managing reputation risk. JPMorgan notes that reputation risk events are introduced by various parties and can lead to harm, implying a need for management. Citi explicitly states it has developed a 'reputation risk framework' that includes a 'risk appetite statement' and key indicators to monitor corporate activities. Citi further details that business segments must escalate potential material reputation risks through specific committees. JPMorgan's disclosure focuses on the definition and consequences, while Citi provides more structural detail on the governance (framework, appetite, escalation) used to manage the same type of risk.",
